          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            \-algebras and their variants are collections of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            important in classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+theory"} measure theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"} probability theory
          %p
            Although
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+space"} measurable space
            (to specify the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+subsets"} measurable subsets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            We assume the law of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            throughout; see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cheng+measurable+space"} Cheng measurable space
            for the constructive theory, and compare also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+locale"} measurable locale
          %h3#short_version Short version
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              \-algebra
            is a collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that is closed under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complementation
            and under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+subsets"} families
          %p
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒫
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P} X
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebra
            under the operations of complementation and of union and intersection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            families. Actually, it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+lattice"} complete
            Boolean algebra, since we can also take unions and intersections of all families. A
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %em countable
            families.
          %h3#long_version Long version
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and a collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subseteq X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            could be:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong ring
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a collection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                which is closed under
                = succeed "ation" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+complement"} relative complement
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finitary
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+subsets"} families
              %ol
                %li
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ∅
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \empty
                  is in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %li
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  are in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                          %mo ∪
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cup T
                %li
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  are in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+complement"} relative complement
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mo ∖
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \setminus S
              %p
                It follows that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                is closed under intersections of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
                finite families and under
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+difference"} symmetric difference
                of finite families:
              %ul
                %li
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  are in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi T
                          %mo =
                          %mi T
                          %mo ∖
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo ∖
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cap T = T \setminus (T \setminus S)
                %li
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  are in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                          %mo ⊎
                          %mi T
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo ∖
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∪
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo ∖
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \uplus T = (T \setminus S) \cup (S \setminus T)
              %p
                We can actually use the latter as an alternative to (2), since
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∪
                        %mi T
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ⊎
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊎
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cup T = (S \uplus T) \uplus (S \cap T)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∖
                        %mi S
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊎
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \setminus S = (S \cap T) \uplus T
                %em some
                set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo =
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∖
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \empty = S \setminus S
              %p#EmptyFamilies
                While the union and symmetric difference of an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+family"} empty family
                belong to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                (both being the empty set), the intersection of an empty family (which is
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                itself) might not. The term ‘ring’ dates from the days when a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
                in algebra was not assumed to be unital; so a ring on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is simply a subring (in this sense) of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+ring"} Boolean ring
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P} X
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
                  \-ring
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a ring (as above)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                which is closed under
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
                of countably infinite families. That is:
              %ol
                %li
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ∅
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \empty
                  is in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %li
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  are in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                          %mo ∪
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cup T
                %li
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  are in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+complement"} relative complement
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mo ∖
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \setminus S
                %li
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 3
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_1, S_2, S_3, \ldots
                  are in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                            %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcap_i S_i
              %p
                Of course, every
                = succeed "-ring" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
                = succeed "-ring" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotence
                of intersection (so that
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi T
                        %mo =
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi T
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi ⋯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cap T = S \cap T \cap T \cap T \cap \cdots
              %p
                The symbol ‘
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
                ’ here is from German ‘Durchschnitt’, meaning intersection; it may be used in many contexts to refer to intersections of countable families.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  \-ring
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a ring (as above)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                which is closed under unions of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countably+infinite+set"} countably infinite
                families. That is:
              %ol
                %li
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ∅
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \empty
                  is in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                %li
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  are in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                          %mo ∪
                          %mi T
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cup T
                %li
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  are in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+complement"} relative complement
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mo ∖
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \setminus S
                %li
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 3
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_1, S_2, S_3, \ldots
                  are in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℳ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                            %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup_i S_i
              %p
                Now (2) is simply redundant;
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ∪
                        %mi T
                        %mo =
                        %mi S
