            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
          %p
            Note that the collection of measurable sets with finite measure (in a given
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+space"} measure space
            = succeed "-ring," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            = succeed "-finite" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "-ring." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %h3#measurable_sets Measurable sets
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+space"} measurable space
            is usually defined to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            on
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            In any case, an
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+subset"} measurable subset
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %strong measurable set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that belongs to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            is one of the more general variations, then we also want some subsidiary notions:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relatively+measurable+subset"} relatively measurable
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cap T
            belongs to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            does, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-measurable+subset"} measurable
            if it is a countable union of elements of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is at least an algebra; in any case, the relatively measurable sets form a (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            )-algebra if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            is at least a (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            )-ring. Similary, every
            = succeed "-measurable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is at least a
            = succeed "-ring;" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "-measurable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            is at least a
            = succeed "-ring." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
          %h3#generating_algebras
            Generating
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            As a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base"} bases
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subbase"} subbases
            of
            = succeed "-algebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topologies
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniformities
            %em is
            quite easy to generate rings or algebras, but generating
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "-algebras.)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            We do get something by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+abstract+nonsense"} general abstract nonsense
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
            of any collection of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "-algebra;" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+closure"} Moore closure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            of sets whatsoever, the intersection of all
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            is a
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %strong generated
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            and similar concepts for all of the other notions defined above.)
          %p
            What is missing is a simple description of the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            can be taken as a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subbase"} subbase
            of an algebra, the symmetric unions of finite families of elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            form a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base"} base
            of the algebra, and the intersections of finite families of elements of the base form an algebra. For a ring, the only difference is to use intersections only of inhabited families. But for anything from a
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            In fact, the question of how to generate a
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descriptive+set+theory"} descriptive set theory
          %ul
            %li
              Start with a collection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_0
              (our collection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
              above), and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
              be the collection of the complements of the members of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_0
            %li
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_1
              be the collection of unions of countably infinite families of sets in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1
              be the collection of their complements (the intersections of countably infinite families of sets in
              = succeed ");" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∪
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_1 \cup \Pi_1
              is not in general a
              = succeed "-algebra." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %li
              Continue by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recursion"} recursively
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
              for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_\omega
              be the union of the various
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_n
              = succeed "-algebra." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %li
              Continue by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+induction"} transfinite
              recursion, defining
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_\alpha
              for all countable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+numbers"} ordinal numbers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            %li
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ω
                          %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_{\omega_1}
              be the union of the various
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_\alpha
              %em this
              is finally a
              = succeed "-algebra." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            So we need an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℵ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_1
            steps, not just
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %p
            (This is only the beginning of descriptive set theory; our
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_\alpha
            are their
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi α
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^0_\alpha
            —except that for some reason they start with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^0_1
            instead of
            = succeed "\u2014," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 0
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^0_0
          %p
            Note that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+choice"} countable choice
            is essential here and elsewhere in measure theory, to show that a countable union of a countable union is a countable union. But the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            is not; in fact, much of descriptive set theory (although this is irrelevant to the small portion above) works better with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+determinacy"} axiom of determinacy
            instead.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Of course, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is closed under all operations, so it is a
                = succeed "-algebra." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %strong
                    Borel
                    = succeed "-algebra" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+sets"} Borel sets
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
                are the Borel sets in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
                with its usual topology.
            %li
              %p
                In the application of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+physics"} statistical physics
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermodynamics"} thermodynamics
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                (typically something like
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^N
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                on the order of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Avogadro%27s+number"} Avogadro's number
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+system"} physical system
                and a macrocanonical phase space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                (typically
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
                or at least
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
                for
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 10
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \lt 10
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
                under this projection of the Borel
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                is a
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entropy"} entropy
                of the system is (theoretically) its information-theoretic entropy with respect to this
                = succeed "-algebra." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %li
              %p
                If a measurable space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{M})
                is equipped with a (positive) measure
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+space"} measure space
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-ideal"} ideal
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                (that is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
                that is also a sub-
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                \-ring). Let a
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/null+set"} null set
                be
                %em any
                set (measurable or not) contained in a set of measure zero; then the null sets form a
                = succeed "-ideal" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
                  \-measurable
                if it is the union of a measurable set and a null set; then the
                = succeed "-measurable" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                %strong completion
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                under
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                is only a
                = succeed "-ring," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
                = succeed "-ring;" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                = succeed "-ideal" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
                and simply declaring by fiat that these are the null sets, as with a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localisable+measurable+space"} localisable measurable space
                %strong completion
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                with respect to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
                (or sometimes with respect to the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delta-filter"} filter
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℱ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
                of
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sets"} full sets
            %li
              %p
                In particular, the
                %strong Lebesgue-measurable
                sets in the real line are the elements of the completion of the Borel
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+measure"} Lebesgue measure
          %h2#alternatives Alternatives
          %p
            We are now learning ways to understand
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+theory"} measure theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability"} probability
            away from the traditional reliance on sets required with
            = succeed "-algebras;" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+space"} measurable space
            for a summary of other ways to define this concept. We still need to know what happens to all of the
            %em other
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient
            measurable spaces in place of sub-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            \-algebras; for example, see explicit quotient in the example of macroscopic entropy above.
          %h2#related_concepts  Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
